{"title":"2009 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1d","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Emily sets up a lemonade stand. She has set-up costs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/59309bdf3e8c0ecbdbe60888412cbbf38bd3e6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$12.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and each cup of lemonade costs her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dfbdbe7579b90dd9628d52d693f145426a423e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> to make. She sells each cup of lemonade for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a52990ff1664f1102b7b1fac4e7b2106f5e0728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Why is it not possible for her to make a profit of exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8877b58d43607a3e63716361e1061cdf7b61c831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$17.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of cups that Emily sells. Like in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c\" title=\"2009 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c\">solution 1 of part c</a>, we can realize that she earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fedeeb8f7b802b36d42838ecd463f06162f98855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> net per cup sold.\n</p><p>Thus, Emily's profit (excluding the set-up cost) would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2b499d1abaa0a9ba00918338de209c988bfac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.60c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. However, her set-up cost would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/59309bdf3e8c0ecbdbe60888412cbbf38bd3e6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$12.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. This means that if her overall profit was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8877b58d43607a3e63716361e1061cdf7b61c831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$17.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, we would have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc005af819dbee88278cc065e65b1e808711686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.60c - 12.00 = 17.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"171\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f6f6086a7be8818e616766e40218c3fab6a366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.60c = 29.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/10792064f8595ce43b19e8ebb0d75b9fd0105530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{29.00}{0.60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>However, we realize that this results in a non-integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, which cannot be the case due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> representing a whole number quantity. Thus, Emily cannot get a profit of exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8877b58d43607a3e63716361e1061cdf7b61c831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$17.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221605\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 57/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 315/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2670/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.430      1 2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    7.430      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37000:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221605 and revision id 285934. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}